Trademarks
----------
CodeWarrior is a trademark of NXP B.V. Freescale is a trademark of NXP B.V.
Other product and company names (including HI-WAVE, P&E Multilink and
PEmicro) are trademarks of their respective owners.

S12 Studio is an independent project. It is not affiliated with, sponsored
by, or endorsed by NXP B.V., Freescale, PEmicro, or any other trademark
owner. These names are used only to describe compatibility: S12 Studio opens
and builds CodeWarrior-format (CodeWarrior S12(X) v5.1) projects and follows
that tool's workflow so that course materials written for it keep working.

The S12 Studio source code contains no NXP, Freescale, Metrowerks or PEmicro
source code, binaries, header/include files or project templates. Register
definitions are generated from the MC9S12XDP512 data sheet.

Listing files (.lst) written by S12 Studio's assembler reproduce the header
lines of CodeWarrior's listings, including its "(c) Copyright Freescale"
line, so that they are byte-for-byte comparable with listings made on a lab
PC. That line is reproduced for compatibility only: the listings are output
of S12 Studio, not a work of Freescale or NXP. Likewise, the assembler and
linker print CodeWarrior's message numbers and texts so that build output
matches what course material describes.

S12 Studio contains no ME 3305 course material; the course's project files
and library belong to their authors. Students open the project folder their
course gives them.
